Decode the Unicode core data table without overlaying a record on it

VSS.Implementation.UCD_Core stores the core character properties as 32-bit
words (Core_Data_Raw_Table), with each field at a fixed bit position counting
from the least significant bit, and then overlays an array of Core_Data_Record
on that table, a packed record whose fields are placed by "at 0 range N .. M".
Such a layout follows the bit and byte order of the machine, so the overlay
reads the right fields only on little-endian targets.

On big-endian s390x it decodes garbage.  The visible effect: Display_Width of
"(", ")", "[", "]" and "{" is 2 instead of 1 (their general category is
Ps or Pe, which lands on a wide East Asian width after the misread), so
anything that lays text out by display width counts them double.  In
Prettier_Ada that made lines holding a bracket pair, a parenthesis pair or a
call break two columns early, and failed three Liblktlang unparsing tests
(unparsing/array_lit, dot_expr and raise_expr) on s390x only.

Decode the raw word with shifts and masks in Extract_Core_Data, the only user
of the table.  It is the same on every machine, and the result on little-endian
targets is unchanged.  Checked on s390x: the three tests pass.

--- a/source/text/implementation/vss-implementation-ucd_utilities.adb
+++ b/source/text/implementation/vss-implementation-ucd_utilities.adb
@@ -4,6 +4,8 @@
 --  SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
 --
 
+with Interfaces;
+
 package body VSS.Implementation.UCD_Utilities is
 
    -----------------------
@@ -15,6 +17,7 @@
       return VSS.Implementation.UCD_Core.Core_Data_Record
    is
       use type VSS.Implementation.UCD_Core.Core_Offset;
+      use type Interfaces.Unsigned_32;
       use type VSS.Unicode.Code_Point;
 
       Block : constant VSS.Implementation.UCD_Core.Core_Index :=
@@ -24,10 +27,36 @@
         VSS.Implementation.UCD_Core.Core_Offset
           (Code mod VSS.Implementation.UCD_Core.Block_Size);
 
+      Raw : constant Interfaces.Unsigned_32 :=
+        VSS.Implementation.UCD_Core.Core_Data_Raw_Table
+          (VSS.Implementation.UCD_Core.Core_Index_Table (Block) + Offset);
+      --  The table holds 32-bit words with the fields at fixed bit positions,
+      --  least significant bit first (see Core_Data_Record).  Decode them
+      --  here instead of overlaying the record on the table: the overlay
+      --  follows the machine's bit and byte order, so on a big-endian target
+      --  (s390x) it gives wrong properties (for instance, "(" and "[" came
+      --  out with wide East Asian width).
+
+      function Field (Low, Width : Natural) return Natural is
+        (Natural (Interfaces.Shift_Right (Raw, Low) and (2 ** Width - 1)));
+
+      function Flag (Pos : Natural) return Boolean is (Field (Pos, 1) = 1);
+
    begin
       return
-        VSS.Implementation.UCD_Core.Core_Data_Table
-          (VSS.Implementation.UCD_Core.Core_Index_Table (Block) + Offset);
+        (GC      => VSS.Implementation.UCD_Core.GC_Values'Val (Field (0, 5)),
+         OLower  => Flag (5),
+         OUpper  => Flag (6),
+         WSpace  => Flag (7),
+         GCB     => VSS.Implementation.UCD_Core.GCB_Values'Val (Field (8, 4)),
+         InCB    => VSS.Implementation.UCD_Core.INCB_Values'Val (Field (12, 2)),
+         ExtPict => Flag (14),
+         WB      => VSS.Implementation.UCD_Core.WB_Values'Val (Field (16, 5)),
+         EA      => VSS.Implementation.UCD_Core.EA_Values'Val (Field (24, 3)),
+         Emoji   => Flag (27),
+         EBase   => Flag (28),
+         EMod    => Flag (29),
+         EPres   => Flag (30));
    end Extract_Core_Data;
 
 end VSS.Implementation.UCD_Utilities;
